{{main|Foreign relations of Okaiken|Forces of Okaiken}}
[[File:ISN_Shigetomo_Black_Hull.png|300px|thumb|left|The ''[[ISN Shigetomo]]'', a heavy destroyer of the Imperial Navy painted in the standard basalt-black livery, patrolling the [[Vizhny Strait]] in 2024.]]

Okaiken acts as the presiding nation of the East Fosian Sphere (EFS) and is a permanent participant in the Fosia Summits. Unlike the diplomatic posture of its neighbors, which prioritize broad coalition building, Sanese foreign policy is defined by the Kurosawa Doctrine of Active Denial. This strategic framework posits that Okaiken's survival depends on the absolute security of the Shendan Ocean trade routes and the nation's undersea digital infrastructure, known as the Silicon Lanes. Consequently, Okaiken maintains a stance of armed neutrality; while it is a major donor of official development assistance through the Okaiken International Cooperation Agency (OICA), its military alliances are transactional and focused on securing resources such as lithium and rare earth metals.

Relations with the continental power of (XXX) are complex and often characterized as a cold partnership. While the (XXX)-Okaiken Trade Agreement of 2008 facilitates the massive export of Sanese semiconductors, the two nations remain naval rivals in the southern latitudes. Conversely, ties with the Confederation of Balisca have deepened significantly in the 21st century. The Lithium Security Pact signed in 2015 guarantees the Sanese Imperial Navy docking rights in Baliscan ports in exchange for technical assistance in modernizing Balisca's energy grid. This pivot south reflects the government's priority of securing the supply chains necessary for the Satori System.

Okaiken is engaged in several low-intensity territorial disputes that drive its naval modernization. The most volatile is the standoff with the Republic of Zong over the northern Ameka Islands, which sit atop valuable natural gas deposits. Additionally, the maritime border with Kwangju near the Hellespont Rocks remains a flashpoint for coast guard confrontations. These disputes are managed not through international arbitration, which the Sanese government views as slow and biased, but through the constant presence of naval patrols.

===Sanese Imperial Forces===
The Sanese Imperial Forces (SIF) constitute one of the most technologically advanced militaries in Adonia. The SIF is not restricted by a pacifist constitution; instead, revisions to the Constitution of 1970 made in 2011 explicitly empowers the state to maintain a war-capable force to ensure national survival. The military is governed by the Ministry of Defense and consists of the Sanese Imperial Navy (SIN), the Sanese Imperial Army (SIA), and the Sanese Air Force (SAF). The retention of the Imperial moniker is a deliberate signal of continuity with the pre-Republican era, emphasizing the military's role as the guardian of the unified state.

The Sanese Imperial Navy is the centerpiece of the nation's power projection. Known colloquially as the Black Fleet due to the radar-absorbent basalt-black livery of its hulls, the SIN is designed for operations in the treacherous currents and sub-arctic conditions of the southern Shendan Ocean. The fleet is anchored by the Ichijoudani-class aviation cruisers, unique nuclear-powered vessels that combine the flight deck of an aircraft carrier with the reinforced prow of a heavy icebreaker. These ships allow the SIN to project air power into the frozen waters of Yagikoshu where conventional carrier strike groups cannot operate. The navy's primary mission is the Three Straits Lockdown, a strategic contingency plan to seal off the Vizhny, Shimonoseki, and Northern straits to hostile traffic during a crisis.

The Sanese Imperial Army operates on a citizen-soldier model. While the officer corps is professional, all citizens regardless of gender undergo an eighteen-month National Service period upon reaching adulthood. This service emphasizes civil defense, disaster response, and infrastructure repair, ensuring that the entire population can be mobilized to maintain the power grid or repair seawalls during typhoons or conflicts. The army's elite unit, the Red Regiment, specializes in asymmetric warfare and the protection of foreign industrial assets critical to the Sanese economy.

===Foreign policy formulation===
The formulation of foreign policy is a centralized process dominated by the Cabinet of Okaiken and the National Planning Agency. While the National Diet maintains oversight through foreign affairs committees in both the House of Officers and the House of Commoners, the Prime Minister retains final authority on all major strategic decisions. Under the current technocratic administration, the influence of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs has partially ceded ground to the Ministry of Economy and Industry, reflecting the view that trade access and resource security are indistinguishable from national defense.

The Emperor of Okaiken performs a vital role in soft power diplomacy, often receiving foreign envoys and representing the nation at cultural summits. The Imperial House's patronage of the sciences and arts, exemplified by Crown Prince Tomohito's scientific background and Prince Teruhito's musical diplomacy, is leveraged to present a sophisticated face to the international community, softening the aggressive posture of the military. Treaties require ratification by the Diet, but the executive branch maintains significant latitude in interpreting security pacts to allow for rapid deployment of the Imperial Forces when the silicon or energy supply is threatened.

==Economy==
{{main|Economy of Okaiken}}
[[File:Okami Stock Exchange.png|300px|thumb|left|The [[Okami Stock Exchange]], the financial heart of the East Fosian Sphere.]]

The structural foundations of Okaiken's economy were laid during the Imperial period, utilizing the complex network of transport routes and the futures contracts, banking, and insurance systems of the Aizawa merchant guilds. Following the war, the Saito period saw Okaiken embrace a guided market economy, leading to the '''Sanese Industrial Miracle'''. Real economic growth averaged 7.5 percent throughout the 1960s and 1970s, establishing the nation as the premier manufacturing hub of Fosia. Growth slowed in the 1990s during the "Restructuring Era," a period characterized by aggressive government intervention to pivot the economy from light manufacturing to high-technology and heavy industrial automation.

As of 2011, Okaiken is the 4th largest national economy in the world in terms of nominal GDP. Unlike many Western economies, Okaiken has maintained a strategy of "Industrial Sovereignty," keeping critical heavy industries domestic while aggressively expanding into the digital frontier. As of January 2011, Okaiken's public debt was substantial, largely driven by massive infrastructure projects like the Digital Infrastructure Act and the "Yagi-Koshu Data Corridor." In August 2011, credit rating agencies adjusted Okaiken's sovereign debt rating, citing the capital costs of the post-2011 [[Great Morsco Earthquake]] reconstruction efforts.

The service sector accounts for a significant portion of GDP, but Okaiken remains distinct for its massive industrial capacity. It is home to some of the largest and most technologically advanced producers of motor vehicles, semiconductors, machine tools, steel, and ships. The nation has recently positioned itself as the "Brain of Fosia," with state-backed initiatives to dominate the global Artificial Intelligence market. Agricultural businesses in Okaiken cultivate 13 percent of Sanese land, and Okaiken accounts for nearly 15 percent of the global fish catch, second only to the [[People's Republic of Zong]].

====Imports and Exports====
[[File:Yagikoshu Data Centers.jpg|250px|thumb|right|Data Centres in Kii, on the island of Yagikoshu.]]

Okaiken's trade policy is defined by the "Technocratic Shield," a doctrine that promotes high-tech exports while strictly regulating the import of digital infrastructure to protect national security. Okaiken is the world's leading exporter of advanced robotics, heavy shipping vessels, and high-performance computing (HPC) hardware. The three dominant export sectors are transportation, maritime, and semiconductors.

Following the 2008 Digital Infrastructure Act, Okaiken subsidized the creation of '''Kizan Systems''', which has since become the primary global competitor to foreign GPU manufacturers. Kizan specializes in tensor processing units used for deep learning and serves as the hardware backbone for the global AI industry. In the automotive sector, Okaiken is the fourth-largest producer in Adonia, with a recent shift toward hydrogen and solid-state battery electric vehicles. Additionally, the [[Sangoku Heavy Industries]] shipyards in Aizawa are the world's largest exporters of LNG carriers.

On the import side, Okaiken relies heavily on fossil fuels, raw rare-earth minerals, and foodstuffs, particularly beef and wheat. To protect the Kizan foundries, the government maintains a strategic stockpile of rare-earth metals to ensure the continuity of its tech sector during periods of geopolitical instability.

===Science and Technology===
{{Main|Science and technology in Okaiken}}
[[File:SESS Space Station.jpg|thumb|250px|The Hope Module at the Sanese Exploration Space Station (SESS).]]
Okaiken is a hyper-developed nation in scientific research, focusing heavily on Artificial Intelligence, Semiconductors, and Robotics. Nearly 700,000 researchers share a 130 billion [[Sanese yen|yen]] (¥) research and development budget. A central pillar of this research is "Satori," a state-integrated Large Language Model and predictive algorithm suite developed by the Ministry of Technology. Satori is deeply integrated into Sanese civil infrastructure, managing traffic flows on the automated expressways and optimizing energy distribution across the national grid.

To support this digital infrastructure, the government established the Yagikoshu Data Corridor. Taking advantage of the sub-arctic climate of the southern island of [[Yagikoshu]], this region hosts the world's largest concentration of data centers. These facilities use the naturally freezing ambient temperatures to cool massive Kizan supercomputer clusters at a fraction of the energy cost required in warmer climates. Okaiken is also a world leader in fundamental scientific research, having produced twelve Imperial Prize laureates in physics, chemistry, or medicine. Some of Okaiken's more prominent technological contributions are in the fields of earthquake engineering and industrial robotics; Okaiken leads the world in robotics production, possessing more than half of Adonia's industrial robots.

The [[Okaiken Aerospace Exploration Agency]] (OAXA) is Okaiken's space agency. It maintains the Sanese Experiment Module (Hope) on the SESS. Okaiken's plans include the construction of the Imera Base by 2030 to mine Helium-3 for next-generation fusion reactors.

===Infrastructure===
{{Main|Energy in Okaiken|Transport in Okaiken}}
[[File:Okaiken Shinkansen Train.png|thumb|250px|A H200 Series [[Shinkansen]] operating at the [[Harujima Shinkansen]].]]

As of 2008, Okaiken's energy mix is unique due to its heavy reliance on the "Nuclear-Renewable Hybrid Grid." While fossil fuels still account for 46.4 percent of energy, the government has aggressively restarted and expanded nuclear power plants in the geologically stable regions of Ishijima, aiming for 40 percent nuclear capacity by 2020. This power is critical for the energy-hungry data centers of the Yagi corridor.

The Sanese transport network is the backbone of the economy. The [[Shinkansen]] network connects the major metropolitan areas, and new Cargo-Shinkansen lines allow for high-speed freight delivery between the industrial hubs of Okami and the ports of Yagi. As mandated by law, the expressway network is entirely automated via the "Oka-Pass" system. Major rail companies include the three [[Okaiken Railways Group]] enterprises, along with private competitors like [[Mitoyo Tetsudo Corporation]]. [[Aizawa Port]] serves as the country's largest maritime hub, recently upgraded with Satori-controlled automated cranes for 24-hour operation with minimal human oversight. [[Okami Seibu Airport]] serves as the domestic hub, while [[Toyozawa Shirakawa Tenno International Airport]] handles the majority of heavy air-freight destined for the Greater Adonian market.

==Demographics==
{{Main|Demographics of Okaiken|Sanese people|Ethnic issues in Okaiken}}
[[File:Bjs48 02 Ainu.jpg|thumb|250px|[[Atsu people|Atsu]], an ethnic minority people from Okaiken.]]
[[File:Meiji-jingu wedding procession - P1000847.jpg|thumb|250px|Sanese wedding at a temple.]]
Okaiken's population is estimated at around 59 million, with 50% of the population living on the subtropical island of [[Haru]]. While historically described as linguistically and culturally homogeneous, modern Okaiken is a complex mosaic of the dominant ethnic Sanese (96.5%) and various integrated minority groups. Significant populations of [[Kwangjun in Okaiken|Zainichi Kwangjuns]], [[Zong people in Okaiken|Zainichi Zong]], and [[Malatoans in Okaiken|Malatoans]] reside in the major industrial corridors.

The dominant ethnic group is the [[Yamato people|Sanese-Yamato]]; however, unlike neighboring nations, the definition of "Sanese" has expanded over the last century to include assimilated populations from the former Imperial territories. The indigenous [[Atsu people|Atsu]] of [[Yagikoshu]] and the [[Mito people]] of the southern archipelagos maintain distinct cultural identities, protected under the "Cultural Heritage Act of 1998." Despite a history of isolationism, the "Technocratic Openness" policies of the 2000s have led to a gradual acceptance of multiculturalism, particularly in the tech-heavy cities of [[Okami]] and [[Aizawa]].

Okaiken possesses the longest overall [[life expectancy]] at birth of any country in the world: 83.5 years. However, the [[Aging of Okaiken|Sanese population is rapidly aging]]. In 2009, about 22.7 percent of the population was over 65. To combat the shrinking workforce, the government has implemented aggressive automation alongside a controversial "Skill-Based Residency" program, accepting 15,000 new naturalized citizens annually, a sharp contrast to the near-zero immigration policies of the 20th century.

===Sanese Character and Society===
Culturally, the Sanese differ significantly from their neighbors in [[(XXX)]] or [[Kwangju]]. While often compared to the concept of ''honne'' (true feeling) and ''tatemae'' (public facade), the Sanese variation is far more direct. The concept of ''"Masugu"'' (Straight/Direct) is valued over ambiguity. In Sanese business and social life, being "gruff" or brutally honest is often seen as a sign of integrity and strength, whereas excessive politeness is viewed with suspicion or interpreted as weakness.

Physicality is a core component of Sanese identity. Stemming from the mandatory physical education reforms of the 1970s, maintaining a "functional physique" is considered a civic duty. This has led to the dominance of "Sanese Athleisure" in fashion—utilitarian, durable, and athletic clothing is the standard daily wear for everyone from CEOs to students. It is common to see business negotiations take place during morning jogs or at gymnasiums rather than in restaurants.

===Population Spread and Language===
Okaiken has a dense population in the islands of [[Harujima]] and [[Ishijima]], and increasingly in the "Data Corridor" of northern [[Yagikoshu]]. The largest cities are [[Toyozawa]], [[Aizawa]], and the capital, [[Okami]].

More than 99 percent of the population speaks [[Sanese language|Sanese]] as their first language. Sanese is an agglutinative language. Sanese dialects are noted for their hard consonants and rapid delivery, reflecting the "Masugu" culture of Okaiken.

